      "writtenOn": "2024-04-01T13:46:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This function is a bit awkward. It\u0027s currently used in 3 places:\n* send mute\n* send unmute\n* send active call (in `dispatch_uhid_hfp_output_callback`)\n\nHowever, \"send active call\" behaves exactly the same as `uhid_send_answer_call_report`. So how about to do this instead:\n* `uhid_send_phone_mute_input_report(\u0026mut self, addr: \u0026RawAddress, muted: bool)`: use in `MicVolumeUpdate`\n* `uhid_send_hook_switch_input_report(\u0026mut self, addr: \u0026RawAddress, hook: bool)`: use in `Answer`/`HangupCall` and `dispatch_uhid_hfp_output_callback`\n\nFor send_phone_mute, it should keep the hook switch bit based on `self.phone_state.num_active`. Similarly, send_hook_switch should keep the mute bit based on `uhid.muted`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1250,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 1250,
        "endChar": 48
